            <h2 class="section-title">Voluntary Resignation (Section 168)</h2>
            <div class="content-text">
                
                <p><strong>Process:</strong> (1) Director submits written resignation letter. (2) Board acknowledges at Board Meeting - no shareholder resolution needed. (3) Company files DIR-12 within 30 days. (4) Director files DIR-11 within 30 days stating reasons. (5) Effective from date received or later date specified.</p><p><strong>Key:</strong> Board CANNOT refuse resignation. Once submitted, it takes effect per its terms.</p><p><strong>Gurugram context:</strong> Preferred route for most changes: co-founders amicably parting, MNC nominees replaced, directors stepping down. Patron drafts resignation letter, Board Resolution, and files DIR-11 + DIR-12. See <a href="/legal-drafting">Legal Drafting</a> for exit agreements.</p>

