                <div class="faq-expanded__list">
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-1">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">How to remove a director?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Shareholders issue special notice (14 days), convene EGM, give director opportunity to be heard, pass Ordinary Resolution. File DIR-12 within 30 days. Or director can resign voluntarily under Section 168. Patron manages both routes.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-2">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Can a director be removed without consent?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Yes. Under Section 169, shareholders can remove by Ordinary Resolution even without consent. Director must be given opportunity to be heard but cannot veto if majority vote in favour.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-3">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What is special notice?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Notice by shareholders to company at least 14 days before meeting proposing removal. Company sends copy to director. Mandatory for Section 169. Without it, removal is procedurally invalid.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-4">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Removal vs resignation difference?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Removal: initiated by shareholders, needs OR + special notice, 21-35 days. Resignation: voluntary by director, effective in 1-7 days. Both need DIR-12. Resignation also needs DIR-11 by director.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-5">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What if director absent 12 months?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Under Section 167(1)(b), deemed automatically vacated after 12 consecutive months Board absence despite receiving notice. No resolution needed. Company files DIR-12.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-6">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Can the Board remove a director?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>No. Power lies solely with shareholders under Section 169. Board cannot pass removal resolution. However, if AoA grants Board such power, courts have allowed in certain cases.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-7">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What forms needed with ROC?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Removal: DIR-12 by company (30 days) with OR, special notice, minutes. Resignation: DIR-12 by company + DIR-11 by director (both 30 days). Vacation: DIR-12 by company with evidence.</p></div>
                    </div>
